    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0453" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/151</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State (Stimson)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-05">January 5, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>During the call of the Guatemalan Minister I asked him about the situation of
                    Guatemala, expressing to him my gratification at the Guatemalan support of the
                    Treaty of 1923. The Minister told me that although the Treaty had been renounced
                    by Costa Rica and Salvador, the other three countries acted to support it, and I
                    said we would support it so long as these Republics did. He then stated that
                    Costa Rica really stood as a nation apart from the others and her action did not
                    make so much difference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">enry</hi>] L.
                                S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">timson</hi>]
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
